<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalinga</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kalinga was an ancient region on the eastern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, roughly corresponding to present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>. It was conquered by the Maurya emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a> in a bloody war. The suffering caused by the conquest is traditionally said to have led Ashoka to embrace <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> and non-violence.</p></div>
